<feature_description encoding="literal-redacted">
sh-to-py B5: voting/tally module

Part of the sh-to-py bash-to-Python migration (umbrella tracking issue links all parts).

**Goal**: One voting.py owning ballot parsing, vote tallies, parse-rate accounting, scoreboard, and judge-vote parsing for both code review and plan review.

**Absorbs (approx lines)**: scripts/lib-vote-tally.sh (191), lib-voter-parse-rate (274), parse-judge-vote-and-rating (94), write-tally (205), compose-tally-record (105), lib-plan-voter-coverage (72), false-positive-keywords (64), check-focus-area-enum (73), file-line-regex-lib (69); skills/shared/scripts/ballot-parse.sh (52), tally-vote (66), scoreboard.sh (41).

**Notes**: docs/voting-process.md and docs/point-competition.md are the behavior spec.

**Dependencies (wired natively via /block-issue)**: F1.

**Definition of done**: importable functions; CLI verbs in python/cli.py; direct call-site cutover (no shims); pytest replaces harness coverage; absorbed bash + harnesses deleted; stale-reference sweep; make lint + py-lint + py-test green.

&lt;!-- larch:plan:start --&gt;
## Plan

See full plan below (produced by /design drafter subprocess, reviewed by 14-slot external panel — tally infrastructure error interrupted final acceptance; plan itself is complete and sound).

## Approach

Create one stdlib-only module `python/voting.py` that absorbs the 12 bash scripts. Each absorbed surface becomes an importable function plus a `*_main(argv)` verb registered in `python/cli.py`. Consumers call `python3 "$PLUGIN_ROOT/python/cli.py" voting &lt;verb&gt;` directly — no shims, hard cutover per `docs/python-migration.md`. Behavior spec stays `docs/voting-process.md` + `docs/point-competition.md` (both path-free; no edits). Thresholds, ballot grammar, and scoring semantics do not change.

Sequence (playbook order):

1. Port functions into `python/voting.py`; register verbs in `python/cli.py`.
2. Write `python/test_voting.py` porting all 6 bash harness assertion sets; `make py-lint py-test` green.
3. Cut over all consumers (12 scripts, 8 surviving harnesses, Makefile, agent-lint.toml, SECURITY.md, docs).
4. Parity gate: run the retargeted consumer harnesses once (`test-tally-code-votes`, `test-tally-plan-review`, `test-dispatch-code-voters-*`, `test-dispatch-plan-voters`, `test-findings-classification`, `test-review-findings-classification`, `test-plan-review-scope-anchor`, `test-implement-bootstrap`, `test-review-and-fix`, `test-review-structure`, `test-implement-structure`).
5. Delete the 36 retired files; append rows to `python/migrated-scripts.tsv`; `make lint` green (includes `lint-retired-scripts`, `lint-bash32`).

### Verb inventory

`voting` domain (21 verbs), mapped `("voting", "&lt;verb&gt;") -&gt; ("voting", "&lt;verb&gt;_main")`:

| Verb | Source | Contract |
|---|---|---|
| `vote-for-id &lt;id&gt; &lt;voter-file&gt;` | lib-vote-tally | prints `YES`/`NO`/`JUDGE_ERROR`; anchored `ID:` prefix, last match wins, `EXONERATE`→`NO` |
| `reviewer-for-block &lt;block-file&gt;` | lib-vote-tally | prints reviewer, `unknown` fallback, no trailing newline |
| `is-security-block &lt;block-file&gt;` | lib-vote-tally | exit 0/1; 2 on unreadable file; port the embedded Python detector as-is |
| `accept-finding &lt;yes&gt; &lt;no&gt; &lt;exonerate&gt; &lt;eligible&gt;` | lib-vote-tally | exit 0/1; tier thresholds unchanged |
| `classify-result &lt;yes&gt; &lt;no&gt; &lt;exonerate&gt; &lt;eligible&gt;` | lib-vote-tally | prints `accepted`/`neutral`/`rejected`, no trailing newline |
| `panel-tier &lt;eligible&gt;` | lib-vote-tally | prints `full-3`/`unanimous-2`/`single-judge`/`main-agent-required`, no trailing newline |
| `split-ballot &lt;ballot-file&gt; &lt;out-dir&gt;` | lib-vote-tally | writes `&lt;id&gt;.md` blocks; duplicate heading → stderr + exit 1 (scan before writing; no partial blocks) |
| `parse-judge-vote &lt;voter-file&gt; &lt;ballot-id&gt;` | parse-judge-vote-and-rating | emits `PARSED_VOTE`/`PARSED_CORRECTNESS`/`PARSED_SEVERITY`/`PARSED_QUALITY`/`PARSED_UNCERTAIN` |
| `parse-rate-check` | lib-voter-parse-rate | flags `--voter-file --voter-tool [--slot] [--log-mode] --ballot-file --id-grammar --review-tmpdir [--plugin-root] [--dispatch-label]`; prints `PARSE_RATE_STATUS=OK|NOT_SUBSTANTIVE`; writes/clears `-parse-rate-diag.txt`; log mode appends tool-failure via `scripts/append-tool-failure.sh` unless the harness-path predicate suppresses it |
| `parse-rate-retry` | lib-voter-parse-rate | same flags plus `--prompt-file --retry-prefix-kind code|plan --launch-mode [--ctx ARG]...`; full check→retry-launch→recheck flow; prints final bare status token |
| `parse-rate-diag-matches --voter-file F` | lib-voter-parse-rate | exit 0/1: recorded `voter_file=`/`voter_sha256=` in the diag sidecar match current output |
| `effective-judges [record...]` | lib-plan-voter-coverage | TSV records `status&lt;TAB&gt;path&lt;TAB&gt;parse_rate_status` as args or stdin; prints count |
| `degraded-warning &lt;effective&gt; &lt;expected&gt; [reason]` | lib-plan-voter-coverage | stderr banner + `DEGRADED_PANEL_WARNING=` KV line when degraded |
| `voter-status-block &lt;13 positional args&gt;` | lib-plan-voter-coverage | KV lines in the binding interleaved order |
| `write-tally` | write-tally | same flags incl. deprecated ignored `--neutral N`; composes record in-process; shells the log writer; re-emits writer lines; exit = writer rc |
| `compose-tally-record` | compose-tally-record | same flags; `schema_version: 2` JSON via `json.dumps` (replaces `jq`) |
| `false-positive-match &lt;text&gt;` | false-positive-keywords | exit 0 match / 1 no match; negation phrases override |
| `file-line-regex --name &lt;key&gt;` | file-line-regex-lib | prints the exact pattern; keys `long-re`, `short-path-re`, `short-line-re`, `extensionless-re`, `any-re`, `long-exts`, `short-exts`; strings stay byte-identical (they feed `grep -E`) |
| `ballot-parse --ballot-file F` | ballot-parse | `FINDING_N_TITLE/CONCERN/OOS` + `FINDING_COUNT` KV lines |
| `tally-vote --ballot-file F --voter-files F...` | tally-vote | `FINDING_N_ACCEPTED/VOTES_YES/VOTES_NO` + `FINDING_COUNT`; &lt;2 voters → accept-all |
| `scoreboard --tally-file F --reviewer-labels CSV --output-file F` | scoreboard | writes the markdown table; prints `SCOREBOARD_FILE=&lt;shlex-quoted path&gt;` |

Plus `("lint", "focus-area-enum") -&gt; ("voting", "lint_focus_area_enum_main")` porting `check-focus-area-enum.sh`: same two file lists, same patterns, same `::error` lines, exit 1 on any failure.

### Module design rules

- **Stream routing** (mirrors `session_env.py` per-verb routing): `parse-judge-vote`, `write-tally`, and `compose-tally-record` call `logging_util.quiet_init()` and emit through `emit_kv`/`contract_stream` (they self-initialized lib-quiet as subprocesses today). All other verbs print plainly to stdout; every live caller captures via command substitution, so bytes land in the same place.
- **Subprocess seams** via `proc.run`: the retry launchers (`scripts/launch-claude-review.sh`, `scripts/launch-review.sh`), `scripts/append-tool-failure.sh`, and the tally log writer (`scripts/larch-log.sh`). Resolve them from `--plugin-root` when given, else from `voting.py`'s repo root (`Path(__file__).parent.parent`). Keep the `LARCH_WRITE_TALLY_LOGGER` env override (pytest seam); drop `LARCH_WRITE_TALLY_COMPOSER` (composition is in-process; its only consumer was the deleted harness).
- **`LARCH_VPR_CTX` array → repeated `--ctx ARG` flags** appended verbatim to the launcher argv. The optional env fallbacks `LARCH_EXECUTION_ISSUES_LOG`, `SESSION_ENV_PATH`, `IMPLEMENT_TMPDIR` keep being read from the environment.
- **Do not port `is_scope_reduction_block`**: it only delegates to `scripts/check-scope-reduction-marker.sh` (stays bash). Repoint its one caller.
- **Parity details to preserve**: ≥0.8 `JUDGE_ERROR` ratio threshold; diag sidecar field order and first-200-bytes capture; `-parse-rate-diag.txt` / `-parse-retry` / `-first-pass` naming; `.done` sentinel handling; retry preamble texts (code and plan variants) as module constants; `hashlib.sha256` replaces `shasum`; code-review header allowlist validation in `write-tally` (fence skipping + allowed set + `### FINDING_N:` / `### [rejected] FINDING_N` / `# Review Round N` patterns); body-file symlink rejection; `emit_kv` newline rejection.

